# openOODA AArch64 std Surface Audit

Logline: Catalog of std/hw/arch_aarch64/ public fns, the oodac/ callers, the must-wire set for the AArch64 AST shim Turn 2, the rename set, and dead symbols.

Setup: Static analysis only. Counts derived from `wc -l` and `grep -l`. No .oo file was modified.

Beats:
  1. Inventory every .oo in std/hw/arch_aarch64/ with line count and one-line role.
  2. Build the external call graph: which std fns are called from oodac/, scripts/, or tests/.
  3. List the must-wire set the AArch64 AST shim Turn 2 will call, citing the emit-ladder arm each replaces.
  4. List the rename set: fns whose names should change in the shim layer for consistency.
  5. List dead symbols: pub fns in std/hw/arch_aarch64/ with zero external callers.
  6. Surface the cross-file risks a shim must navigate.

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-std-surface.oot
Static analysis only. Inventory 2026-08-25.

---

## 1. std/hw/arch_aarch64/ file inventory

125 .oo files, 10,541 lines total (`wc -l std/hw/arch_aarch64/*.oo`, verified 2026-08-25). The directory exists at `ooda/std/hw/arch_aarch64/`. The pre-existing audit `aarch64-investigations.oot:60` claims 394,829 lines; the deep-dive at `audit/aarch64-deep-dive.oot:38` already flags this as 37x drift.

